NATIONAT ASSEM BLY SECRETARIAT
ORDERS OF THE DAYfor the meeting of the National Assembly to be held on Wednesday, the 15th January, 2025 at 2.00 p.m.
Tilowat, Hodith, Noot and national anthem.QUESTIONS
2. Questions entered in a separate list to be asked and answers given.
3, MS. ASIYA NAZ TANOLI MS, ZAHRA WADOOD FATEMIMS. NUZHAT SADIq to invite attention of the Minister for National Health Services, Regulationsand Coordination to a matter of urgent public importance regarding spread of human metapneumo virus in thecountry, causing grave concern amongst the public.
MOTION
4. MS. HINA RABBANI KHAR, Chairperson Standing Committee on Foreign Affairs to move that delay inpresentation of report of the Standing Committee on the Bill to give effect to the Convention on the Prohibitionof the Development, Production and Stockpiling of Eacteriological (Biological) and Toxin Weapons and on theirDestruction, L972 lThe Baological and Toxin Weapons Convention (lmplementation) Bil, 20241, till today becondoned.PRESENTATION OF REPORT OF THE STANDING COMMITTEE
5. MS. HINA RABBANI KHAR, Chairperson Standing Committee on Foreign Affairs to present the report ofthe Standing Committee on the Bill to give effect to the Convention on the Prohibition of the Development,Production and Stockpiling of Bacteriological (Biological) and Toxin Weapons and on their Destruction, 1972[The Biological and Toxin Weapons Convention (lmplementation) Bil,20241.MOTION OF THANKS
5. Further discussion on the following motion moved by SENATOR AZAM NAZEER TARAR, Minister forLaw and Justice and Parliamentary Affairs on 24th April,2024-
"This House expresses its deep gratitude to the President of Pakistan for his address to both Housesassembled together on 18th April, 2024."MATTERS OTHER THAN POINTS OF ORDER
7.
Raising matters under Rule 18 which are not Points of Order
cAtL[lG 4IlENIlqN N oTtCE
8, MS. ALIYA KAMRAN to invite attention of the Minister for National Health Services,Regulations and Coordination to a matter of urgent public importance regarding shortage of medicalequipment, including essential items like ventilators, testing machines and Genexpert systems, in PIMS,lslamabad, the Federal Government Polyclinic, lslamabad and other federally administered hospitals, causinggrave concern amongst the public.
TAHIR HUSSAINSecretary General
CALLING ATTENTION NOTICE
lslamabad, the14th Januarv, 2025

